#!/usr/bin/env python
"""Apply a list of node-level edits to LIVE published Substack posts, in place.

    python SCRIPTS/substack/live_edit.py plan.json            # dry run, prints the diff
    python SCRIPTS/substack/live_edit.py plan.json --live     # writes, then re-reads and asserts

Why: `substack.py update` regenerates a whole body from markdown. This edits the
existing live ProseMirror JSON instead, so widgets, buttons, embeds, captions
and image urls that the edit does not name stay byte-identical, and
`post_date`, `email_sent_at`, slug and title never move.

plan.json is a list of {"id": <post id>, "ops": [...]}. Every op names its
target by the node's index in the CURRENT live body and carries an `expect`
guard. All targets resolve before any op runs, so indices never shift under a
later op. A guard that fails aborts that whole post and writes nothing.

Any op may use "find": "<unique substring>" (plus optional "type") instead of "index",
and move_after may use "after_find". Content targeting survives earlier edits to the post.

Ops:
  {"op": "remove",  "index": i, "expect": "<substring of src or text>"}
  {"op": "caption", "index": i, "expect": "<src substring>", "text": "new caption"}
  {"op": "insert_after", "index": i, "expect": "<text/src substring>", "node": NODE}
  {"op": "move_after", "index": i, "expect": "...", "after": j, "after_expect": "..."}
  {"op": "replace_image", "index": i, "expect": "<src substring>", "file": "local.png"}
  {"op": "heading_text", "index": i, "expect": "<old heading text>", "text": "New Heading"}
  {"op": "replace_text", "old": "exact text", "new": "replacement"}
     (old must sit inside exactly one text node of the post)
  {"op": "list_start", "find": "...", "type": "ordered_list", "start": 5}
  {"op": "link_href", "find": "...", "old": "<href substring>", "new": "https://..."}

NODE is one of:
  {"youtube": "<videoId>"}        {"tweet": "<status url>"}
  {"substack_post": "<any Substack post url>"}   (embeddedPost card)
  {"paragraph": "text", "link": "<optional url for the whole text>"}
  any raw ProseMirror node dict (must carry "type")

Backups of the full pre-edit record land in SUBSTACK/_LINK-ENGINE/backups/.
